<!--
  Gesture navigation bar geometry for our short screen (mind_one; 15.09 F4459, extended 15.09
  evening).

  WHY: a photo of the keyboard on the device shows a dead strip under it, holding only the gesture
  pill. That strip is the navigation bar inset: the IME window is laid out above it, so the
  keyboard can never reach the bottom edge. AOSP reserves 48dp for it
  (frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/dimens.xml:62), and everything else follows:

      navigation_bar_frame_height   -> @dimen/navigation_bar_height   (the inset windows resize around)
      navigation_bar_gesture_height -> @dimen/navigation_bar_frame_height (bottom swipe start area)

  48dp is a normal-phone figure. Our usable height is 523dp (480 x 551dp at density 360, minus the
  status bar - measured in F4014, see the LatinIME overlay next door), so the stock bar eats 9.2% of
  the screen for a handle that is drawn ~2dp thick.

  FIRST PASS (15.09 day) set navigation_bar_height to 24dp. Because of the chain above that moved
  all three numbers at once, which halved the dead strip but could not remove it: the inset and the
  swipe area were still the same number, and the swipe area cannot go to zero.

  SECOND PASS (15.09 evening, requirement: "remove the empty space under the keyboard, and the white bar
  too"): break the chain and set the two independently.

      navigation_bar_frame_height   = 0dp   -> no inset at all, so the keyboard and every app
                                               reach the physical bottom edge
      navigation_bar_gesture_height = 24dp  -> the bottom swipe START region is unchanged from the
                                               first pass, so home/back gestures behave exactly as
                                               they do today
      navigation_bar_height         = 24dp  -> left alone; it is what three-button mode lays out
                                               against, and that is the fallback if gestures ever
                                               misbehave

  The pill itself is removed separately and without touching geometry - see the SystemUI colors
  overlay next door, which paints the handle transparent.

  🔴 Not verified on the device before the build: resource overlays only take effect in a built
  image, so this is the one change here that ships untested. If the home swipe stops working, the
  way out needs no rebuild - Settings > System > Gestures > System navigation > three-button mode.
  And the single number to raise is navigation_bar_gesture_height.
-->
<resources>
    <dimen name="navigation_bar_height">24dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="navigation_bar_height_landscape">24dp</dimen>

    <!-- The inset apps and the IME are laid out above. Zero = no dead strip. -->
    <dimen name="navigation_bar_frame_height">0dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="navigation_bar_frame_height_landscape">0dp</dimen>

    <!-- Explicit, because it would otherwise inherit the 0dp above and take the gestures with it. -->
    <dimen name="navigation_bar_gesture_height">24dp</dimen>
</resources>
